  "question": {
    "text": "If a circle $\\mathrm{C}$ passing through $(4,0)$ touches the circle $x^2+y^2+4 x-6 y-12=0$ externally at a point $(1,-1)$, then the radius of the circle $\\mathrm{C}$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "JC1b7",
      "text": "\n5\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "TRY0y",
      "text": "\n$2 \\sqrt{5}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Yn7Mo",
      "text": "\n4\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CmRdX",
      "text": "\n$\\sqrt{57}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let A be the centre of given circle and $\\mathrm{B}$ be the centre of circle C.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/CRII0vm6U0ICz7C6oleW7yTn3XvNIYtn88sF4N5r3Q0.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& x^2+y^2+4 x-6 y-12=0 \\\\\n& \\therefore A=(-2,3) \\text { and } B=(g, f)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nNow, from the figure, we have\n$$\n\\frac{-2+g}{2}=1 \\text { and } \\frac{3+f}{2}=-1\n$$\n(By mid point formula)\n$$\n\\Rightarrow g=4 \\text { and } f=-5\n$$\nNow, required radius\n$$\n=\\mathrm{OB}=\\sqrt{9+16}=\\sqrt{25}=5\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
